Command Runs the query? Gives you <code>EXPLAIN</code> No The planner's estimated plan and costs <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> Yes Estimates + actual rows, time, loops <code>EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)</code> Yes Also shared buffer hits/reads (memory vs disk I/O) <pre><code>EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 42;
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 42;
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS, VERBOSE, SETTINGS, FORMAT JSON) SELECT ...;  -- JSON: paste into explain.dalibo.com
</code></pre> <p><code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> really executes the statement. For <code>INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE</code>, roll back:</p> <pre><code>BEGIN;
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) DELETE FROM orders WHERE created_at &lt; now() - interval '2 years';
ROLLBACK;
</code></pre> <p>Always use <code>BUFFERS</code>; the time alone hides whether you were slow because of disk or CPU.</p>

Commande Exécute la requête ? Ce que vous obtenez <code>EXPLAIN</code> Non Le plan et les coûts estimés par le planificateur <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> Oui Estimations + réels : lignes, temps, boucles <code>EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)</code> Oui Aussi les hits/reads des shared buffers (mémoire vs I/O disque) <pre><code>EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 42;
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 42;
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS, VERBOSE, SETTINGS, FORMAT JSON) SELECT ...;  -- JSON : à coller dans explain.dalibo.com
</code></pre> <p><code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> exécute réellement l'instruction. Pour <code>INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE</code>, faites un rollback :</p> <pre><code>BEGIN;
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) DELETE FROM orders WHERE created_at &lt; now() - interval '2 years';
ROLLBACK;
</code></pre> <p>Utilisez toujours <code>BUFFERS</code> ; le temps seul ne dit pas si vous étiez lent à cause du disque ou du CPU.</p>
